Initial extraction: sinter shared local-LLM engine module

Extract the local inference engine (tensor, mlx, llm packages) from
sprout (pkg/gomlx + pkg/tensor nested modules) and auto-term's fork into
the standalone sprout-foundry/sinter module,
merging auto-term's fork-only additions:

- qwen2 architecture (Qwen2.5-Coder support, incl. QKV bias path in
  Linear that qwen3 dropped)
- SINTER_BACKEND env override for backend selection in tensor/detect
- GGML portability: bionic/Termux aligned-alloc fallback, CPU-backend
  registration fallback, GOMLX_GGML_CPU device override

Layout changes from sprout's tree:
- single module (no nested go.mod/replace dance for tensor/ggml)
- model catalog moved to llm/catalog subpackage (apps may keep their
  own catalog; engine no longer ships a hardcoded list)
- new llm/all blank-import package registering every architecture and
  the MLX backend

Env vars renamed SPROUT_*/AUTOTERM_* -> SINTER_*.

Name: sintering fuses metal powder into a dense solid part under heat -
quantized 4-bit weights fused into a running model, on Metal.

Consumed by sprout and auto-term via a local replace directive until
the repo is pushed and tagged.
